{
  "id": "openrulebench-dblp",
  "pillar": "logic",
  "statement": "The input att is a list of [document, attribute, value] rows, as OpenRuleBench's DBLP benchmark stores a bibliography in one attribute relation. The program's value is every row of its query, answer(Id, T, A, Y, M) :- att(Id, title, T), att(Id, year, Y), att(Id, author, A), att(Id, month, M), each as [id, title, author, year, month], in any order.",
